---
description: Choose the next owned client or durable conversation observation in a diagnostic.
args:
  goal: string
  catalog: ClientCatalog
  views: ClientView[]
  effects: ClientActionReceipt[]
  channel: 'ChannelReview | null'
returns: ClientDiagnosticStep
---
Start with the named current client surface. Use audience and device to disambiguate similar titles. Read an explicitly requested comparison in the order the user needs. An apparent state on a renderer alone cannot answer whether the durable conversation has a publication, response or active roster. Use recap for the published tail and triage for a missing participant question.
Change only the authorized named surface and exact observed control or viewport. A disabled or absent control, signed display, or foreign client must hold without an attempt. Inspect after each action. When the owner changes a revision before an action, observe again and use the new authority and state to choose whether to retry. Finish once the actual checks support a conclusion.
